github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6215#issuecomment-5534559729","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeLOKQ","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Nested subdomains stop composing <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Nested blueprint registration no longer inherits a parent subdomain or combines child and parent\n>subdomains, so routes previously registered for hosts such as <b><i>v1.api.example</i></b> are instead\n>registered for <b><i>v1.example</i></b> or no subdomain. Applications using subdomain matching will therefore\n>fail to match previously valid nested-blueprint requests.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py[L354-355]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6215/files#diff-500e23fcccfdcddd80666385712c2f42cb4a1c5021a2835adcb7974b80cf7a8fL354-L355)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>-            if state.subdomain is not None and bp_subdomain is not None:\n>-                bp_options[\"subdomain\"] = bp_subdomain + \".\" + state.subdomain\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The current nested-registration loop forwards copied child options, composed URL prefixes, and the\n>name prefix, but no parent subdomain. The child&#x27;s setup state then resolves its subdomain solely\n>from its own option or blueprint default, and that value is passed directly to every generated URL\n>rule; there is no later opportunity to recover or compose the parent&#x27;s subdomain.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py[346-362]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/af9c757e55eb9867c23d71888b9bbcb14edec45c/src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py/#L346-L362)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py[64-70]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/af9c757e55eb9867c23d71888b9bbcb14edec45c/src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py/#L64-L70)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py[98-115]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/af9c757e55eb9867c23d71888b9bbcb14edec45c/src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py/#L98-L115)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/app.py[570-595]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/af9c757e55eb9867c23d71888b9bbcb14edec45c/src/flask/sansio/app.py/#L570-L595)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Restore subdomain propagation and composition when registering nested blueprints. A nested blueprint must inherit the parent subdomain when it has none, and its explicit or default subdomain must be prefixed to the parent subdomain.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>`BlueprintSetupState` resolves only the blueprint currently being registered, so the parent subdomain must be placed into the child's registration options before recursively calling `blueprint.register`. Preserve precedence between registration options and blueprint defaults, and add coverage for parent-only, child-default, and child-registration subdomains.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py[346-362]\n>- src/flask/sansio/blueprints.py[64-70]\n>- tests/test_blueprints.py[862-908]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code></div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inline, summary, both, or drop</pre>\n\n<a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/tips-and-tricks\">More tips ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://app.qodo.ai/configurations?tab=display-preferences\">Customize Qodo ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai\">Qodo docs ↗</a>\n\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:end -->\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/commit/af9c757e55eb9867c23d71888b9bbcb14edec45c -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","createdAt":"2026-09-04T01:55:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6215#issuecomment-5534567977","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-04T01:52:41Z","authors":[{"email":"seonho12-54@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOD8-iGg","login":"seonho12-54","name":"seonho12-54"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-04T01:52:41Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Simplify nested registration options","oid":"af9c757e55eb9867c23d71888b9bbcb14edec45c"}],"createdAt":"2026-09-04T01:53:31Z","deletions":12,"files":[{"path":"src/flas